cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scQC in your work, please cite it."
title: "scQC: a reproducible quality-control pipeline for single-cell and single-nuclei RNA-seq"
abstract: >-
  scQC separates deriving quality-control thresholds from applying them. Every parameter
  carries a class recording whether it was fixed by the pipeline, derived from the data,
  declared in advance, or adjudicated by a human, and every removal requires a recorded
  approval and remains recoverable. Thresholds that can be measured are measured per cohort
  rather than transferred: count floors from the density valley between the debris and cell
  modes, and the mitochondrial ceiling per library from its own dispersion, at a multiple the
  cohort's own Tukey fences calibrate. Checks that a removal has fallen unevenly across the
  arms of the experimental design run at every step that removes.
authors:
